Silo patch 0035 — DualSense: settings and logs in Silo's folders, not MacGameFix's

Silo's own change on top of 0019-0034 (MacGameFix's DualSense series). Those read their settings from
~/Library/Application Support/MacGameFix (pad.conf, pad.d/<Steam app id>.conf, pad-exes.conf), which MacGameFix's app
writes, and keep their log, the haptics socket and the trigger markers in /tmp/macgamefix-<uid>. In Silo, Silo writes
the settings, from each game's settings: here they are read from ~/Library/Application Support/Silo/DualSense and the
rest goes to /tmp/silo-dualsense-<uid>, so a Silo runtime and a CrossOver with MacGameFix's modules never read each
other's settings or share a socket. Only those two paths change, in code and in the comments that name them.

